error[E0611]: `?` inside a `defer` has nowhere to send its error
 --> mem:///main.lu:6:28
  |
6 |     defer print("deferred {key(ok)?}")
  |     ----- the `defer` runs as `under` leaves
  |                            ^^^^^^^^ this would leave `under` while `under` is already leaving
  |
  = note: a deferred expression runs while the function is leaving, so a second error has nowhere
    to go: handle it inside the `defer` with `else`, or move the fallible call out of the
    `defer` into the body.
